invariant: INV-39
file: srv_handshake.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-blocking server answers a ClientHello that has bytes after
  it in its record with a ServerHello, and reads those bytes under the
  client's handshake key afterwards. RFC 9846 section 5.1 makes that
  unexpected_message. test/tcp_blocking_loop_test.c adds one byte to the
  ClientHello's record and requires that alert in the clear and nothing
  else.

--- old
    // The read key changes after the ServerHello, so this hello must end
    // its record (hsr_check_record_end).
    rc = hsr_check_record_end(h);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
